I'm sure he's cheating on me.

267
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,380
Why else wouldn't he call?

268
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,780
But you two are on a break.

269
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,360
Theoretically, he can do whatever he likes.

270
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:35,840
He's the love of my life.

271
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:37,500
I really messed this up.

272
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:38,780
Come on, hon.

273
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,000
Pull yourself together.

274
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,680
It's going to be all right.

275
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:53,020
But I still love him and it's all my fault.

276
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:55,860
I can't believe how immature and selfish I was being.

277
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,730
I mean, he is a firefighter.

278
00:12:59,530 --> 00:13:03,590
It's not like he can just leave someone in a burning building and meet me for dinner.

279
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,560
I totally messed this up.

280
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,230
You know what, Veronica?

281
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,590
I think you should make the first step.

282
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,450
I'm sure he'll forgive you.

283
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:17,120
No, this is not going to happen.

284
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:20,120
I ruined everything.

285
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:21,970
Hey, do you hear something?

286
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:29,800
Guess what, it's your lovely firefighter.

287
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:55,720
Don't you know I sit around with my head hanging down and I wonder who...

288
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,060
Okay, I really like this dialogue.

289
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:57,800
It's so romantic.

290
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,320
Yeah.

291
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,260
It's romantic but at the same time romantic.

292
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,560
So we want to know what you think will happen next.

293
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:05,560
Yeah, will they get back together?

294
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:06,660
Will they get married?

295
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:07,820
Will they have a baby?

296
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:09,260
Maybe they'll break up forever.

297
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,360
Maybe she'll move halfway across the world.

298
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:16,440
Anything can happen so let us know what you think will happen.

299
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:21,320
Come to our website at EnglishPod.com and leave your comments on the lesson page.

300
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,280
Exactly, and maybe you'll be right.

301
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:24,360
Yeah, you never know.

302
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,660
Okay, so we're out of time for today.

303
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,040
I hope you guys had fun and we'll see you next time.

304
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,240
Until then, it's goodbye.

305
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:39,465
Bye.
